# Rosetta per-runner operator exclusions (RosettaHarnessAlignmentWorkOrder.md §4.4):
# corpus operators that one port's runner does not run. File-level native
# exclusions stay in native.exclude.
#
#   <port>[:<runner>]  <source>  <token>  <reason>
#
# port:   c python swift rust go zig java kotlin csharp csharp-bid
# runner: core wrapper (without a runner, every runner of the port)
# source: dectest fptest intel native
# token:  dectest / fptest / intel: a token the <source>.map includes;
#         native: a canonical op name (the first token of a native line)
# reason: required, the rest of the line. Remove the line when it no longer holds.
# Fields are tab-separated. Checked by rosetta/check_rosetta.py.

# Java's public API has no unsigned integer type, so it exposes signed
# conversions only (decimal128-workorder WrapperLayer.md §4.8, §7.1(4)). The Java
# core runs these; the wrapper cannot. The same holds for the native fitsUInt64
# predicate (15 lines of native/fits.txt).
java:wrapper	intel	bid128_to_uint64_ceil	no public unsigned type: Java exposes signed integer conversions only (WrapperLayer.md §4.8)
java:wrapper	intel	bid128_to_uint64_floor	no public unsigned type: Java exposes signed integer conversions only (WrapperLayer.md §4.8)
java:wrapper	intel	bid128_to_uint64_int	no public unsigned type: Java exposes signed integer conversions only (WrapperLayer.md §4.8)
java:wrapper	intel	bid128_to_uint64_rnint	no public unsigned type: Java exposes signed integer conversions only (WrapperLayer.md §4.8)
java:wrapper	intel	bid128_to_uint64_rninta	no public unsigned type: Java exposes signed integer conversions only (WrapperLayer.md §4.8)
java:wrapper	intel	bid128_to_uint64_xceil	no public unsigned type: Java exposes signed integer conversions only (WrapperLayer.md §4.8)
java:wrapper	intel	bid128_to_uint64_xfloor	no public unsigned type: Java exposes signed integer conversions only (WrapperLayer.md §4.8)
java:wrapper	intel	bid128_to_uint64_xint	no public unsigned type: Java exposes signed integer conversions only (WrapperLayer.md §4.8)
java:wrapper	intel	bid128_to_uint64_xrnint	no public unsigned type: Java exposes signed integer conversions only (WrapperLayer.md §4.8)
java:wrapper	intel	bid128_to_uint64_xrninta	no public unsigned type: Java exposes signed integer conversions only (WrapperLayer.md §4.8)
java:wrapper	native	d128_fitsUInt64	no public unsigned type: Java exposes fitsInLong only (WrapperLayer.md §4.8)

# TEMPORARY (PowHugeIntegerExponentWorkOrder.md Phase 2): bid128_pow is included
# for every port; its huge-integer-y lines need the fix. Each line goes when its
# port takes the fix (Phase 3).
c	intel	bid128_pow	TEMPORARY: pow huge-integer-y fix not yet in this port (PowHugeIntegerExponentWorkOrder.md Phase 3)
python	intel	bid128_pow	TEMPORARY: pow huge-integer-y fix not yet in this port (PowHugeIntegerExponentWorkOrder.md Phase 3)
rust	intel	bid128_pow	TEMPORARY: pow huge-integer-y fix not yet in this port (PowHugeIntegerExponentWorkOrder.md Phase 3)
zig	intel	bid128_pow	TEMPORARY: pow huge-integer-y fix not yet in this port (PowHugeIntegerExponentWorkOrder.md Phase 3)
go	intel	bid128_pow	TEMPORARY: pow huge-integer-y fix not yet in this port (PowHugeIntegerExponentWorkOrder.md Phase 3)
java	intel	bid128_pow	TEMPORARY: pow huge-integer-y fix not yet in this port (PowHugeIntegerExponentWorkOrder.md Phase 3)
kotlin	intel	bid128_pow	TEMPORARY: pow huge-integer-y fix not yet in this port (PowHugeIntegerExponentWorkOrder.md Phase 3)
csharp	intel	bid128_pow	TEMPORARY: pow huge-integer-y fix not yet in this port (PowHugeIntegerExponentWorkOrder.md Phase 3)
csharp-bid	intel	bid128_pow	TEMPORARY: pow huge-integer-y fix not yet in this port (PowHugeIntegerExponentWorkOrder.md Phase 3)
